With these two changes in place:

- Clicking a breadcrumb will still try `findRoot(planeId)` and `findRoot(id)`, but if neither exists it grabs the shape directly from the `elementRegistry` and hands that to `canvas.setRootElement(...)` instead of `undefined`.
- Clicking the drill-in button on a collapsed subprocess likewise will fall back to the shape itself if the plane lookup fails, avoiding the “rootElement required” exception.
